WEBVTT

00:00:00.589 --> 00:00:05.275
Motherboards must provide physical slots and electrical PCI Express lanes suitable for the

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:06.040
chosen GPUs.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.240
A full-length connector may operate with fewer lanes than its shape suggests.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.255
Consult platform documentation rather than assuming every slot is equivalent.

00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:16.170
Physical spacing is often the first constraint.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.010
Large coolers can block neighboring slots, cables, or airflow.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.810
Chassis dimensions, card length, thickness, support brackets,

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.800
and connector clearance must be checked together.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.760
Power-supply planning includes total capacity, transient demand, efficiency,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.175
connector type, cable limits, CPU and storage load, and margin.

00:00:31.175 --> 00:00:34.760
Do not improvise unsafe adapters or overload household circuits.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.230
Follow hardware-vendor and electrical guidance.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.960
Cooling must remove sustained heat from every card, the CPU, memory, storage,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.200
and power components.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.695
One GPU can feed hot exhaust into another.

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:49.097
Airflow path, fan behavior, ambient temperature, dust filters, and noise targets matter.

00:00:49.097 --> 00:00:53.855
Risers and external-GPU arrangements can solve spacing or experimentation needs but add

00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:54.285
bandwidth,

00:00:54.285 --> 00:00:58.080
enclosure, cable, power, compatibility, and support considerations.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.720
They should be treated as distinct architectures, not invisible extensions.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.980
Mixed GPUs complicate memory balance, speed, features, driver support, precision,

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:06.830
and scheduling.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.520
Workstation platforms may offer more lanes, spacing, memory,

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.480
and management than consumer systems, but they add cost.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.570
Choose around the measured workload.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:18.065
Platform topology includes how slots connect to the CPU, chipset, and memory.

00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:21.720
Shared links or indirect paths can affect transfer and peer communication.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.760
Read the motherboard and processor lane diagrams before purchase.
